message: >-
  If you use EnCoDaPy in your work, please cite the Zenodo release and this
  software package.
title: 'EnCoDaPy - Energy Control and Data Preparation in Python'
type: software
version: 0.9.3 # x-release-please-version
date-released: '2026-07-02'  # x-release-please-date
repository-code: https://github.com/gewv-tu-dresden/encodapy
url: https://gewv-tu-dresden.github.io/encodapy/
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21130839
license: BSD-3-Clause
abstract: >-
  EnCoDaPy (Energy Control and Data Preparation in Python) is a modular Python
  framework for the real-time management and optimisation of decentralised
  energy systems. Its modular and extensible architecture supports the development,
  validation and operation of control strategies for energy systems. The
  framework provides structured configuration management, supports interfaces
  such as MQTT, FIWARE and file-based systems, and uses Pydantic-based models
  for robust data validation. The core of the framework is the module for analyzing
  and managing energy systems. EnCoDaPy is open source and is designed for
  researchers, engineers and practitioners in energy system modelling and
  optimisation.

keywords:
  - energy systems
  - sector coupling
  - data analysis
  - control
  - optimization
  - FIWARE
  - MQTT
  - Python
  - Pydantic
